ld64 253.9: fold GCC's Darwin __TEXT,__text_* function subsections into __text

GCC's darwin_function_section places cold code in __text_cold, main and
static constructors in __text_startup, and hot/exit code in __text_hot and
__text_exit (plus *_coal forms). ld64's branch_island pass builds PPC islands
only within one section, so once __text passes the 16 MB bl range a branch
into one of those sections cannot be reached at all. Measured 2026-11-05
linking a native GCC 15.3 cc1plus for 10.5 PPC: "bl PPC branch
out of range (25269676 max is +/-16MB): from ... to
__ZSt20__throw_length_errorPKc" -- the static libstdc++ throw helpers are
cold, so every far call into them failed. ld64 already folds __textcoal_nt
and __StaticInit into __text for the same kind of reason; this extends it.
Applied by hand in darwin-cross/src-cctools, like 0004.

diff --git cctools/ld64/src/ld/ld.cpp cctools/ld64/src/ld/ld.cpp
index 6e3c0f8..3b3b19c 100644
--- a/cctools/ld64/src/ld/ld.cpp
+++ b/cctools/ld64/src/ld/ld.cpp
@@ -241,6 +241,13 @@ const ld::Section& InternalState::FinalSection::outputSection(const ld::Section&
 					return _s_TEXT_text;
 				else if ( strcmp(sect.sectionName(), "__StaticInit") == 0 )
 					return _s_TEXT_text;
+				// GCC's Darwin function subsections (darwin.cc
+				// darwin_function_section): branch islands are only built
+				// within one section, so on PPC a __text past the 16 MB bl
+				// range cannot reach a separate __text_cold/__text_startup
+				// at all (patch 0008).
+				else if ( strncmp(sect.sectionName(), "__text_", 7) == 0 )
+					return _s_TEXT_text;
 			}
 			break;
 		case ld::Section::typeNonLazyPointer:
